Now these I quite like.

#threaten
what monster would you like to threaten?  (Since there may be more
than one nymph, e.g.)
The hill orc fearfully hands over $30 and an orcish helm.
(not reccomended for lawfuls--and possibly neutrals)

#threaten
what moster would you like to threaten?
The gray dragon gets angry!

#plead
with what monster would you like to plead?
the gray dragon offers not to attack you in exchange for $1000, a wand
of lightning, and 3 potions of holy water (based on your inventory;
if you don't have anything good, the monster will refuse your plea).
Accept?

(this command would be OK for all alignments, but would violate the
chivalric code...a no-no for knights.  It would work only on
intelligent monsters, and a successful plea would make the monster
become peaceful)

#barter
with what monster would you like to barter?
What would you like to offer? i
In exchange for a long sword, the dwarf offers you:
a) a dwarvish short sword
b) a dwarvish cloak
c) 20 gold pieces.

Which would you like (- to call off the barter).

This would of course only work with peaceful monsters.  They'd only
offer you things that they considered of lesser value than what you
were offering them.
 
